			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1103,
				20
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Stub Air client and DTOs for update/metrics IPC contract\n\nIntroduce a complete set of stub types and a placeholder client implementation for the Air daemon sidecar in `Source/Air/AirServiceTypesStub`. This prepares the `Vine` protocol contract for background services including update management, file indexing, authentication, and metrics collection.\n\nThe new module defines request and response DTOs for operations like `CheckForUpdates`, `DownloadFile`, `IndexFiles`, and `GetMetrics`, adhering to the project's PascalCase naming convention. The `AirClientType` struct provides a feature-flagged stub implementation that returns a descriptive error when the `AirIntegration` feature is disabled, allowing the build to proceed without the actual daemon link.\n\nThis scaffolding enables the definition of gRPC contracts and type safety between Mountain and the future Air sidecar before the integration logic is implemented.",
			"SHA": "27ceae2065f32f43709f6bf8d14e7ddabe008e57"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T06:33:37Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1082,
				3
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Implement secret management RPC handlers for extension host\n\nIntroduce three new gRPC handlers in `CocoonService` to fulfill the `Vine` protocol contract for secure credential storage and retrieval. This adds `StoreSecret`, `GetSecret`, and `DeleteSecret` implementations in the `Secret` module, bridging the extension host (Cocoon) with the OS keychain via `CommonLibrary::Secret::SecretProvider`.\n\nEach handler marshals requests from the protobuf layer to the underlying `SecretProvider` trait methods, using an empty string for the app name as the service scope. The implementation handles optional values in `GetSecret` by returning an empty string if not found, and maps all trait errors to `Status::internal` with structured logging for debugging.\n\nThese handlers complete the secure storage IPC contract, enabling extensions to persist API keys and tokens securely within the native environment.",
			"SHA": "1b90bde2b886fa341a3f60d6d5483a64475e02c6"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T06:33:21Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1078,
				5
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Implement output channel management handlers\n\nIntroduce the complete set of RPC handlers in `CocoonService` for the `Vine` protocol to bridge the extension host with the Sky UI for output channel operations. This adds handlers for `CreateOutputChannel`, `AppendOutput`, `ClearOutput`, `DisposeOutput`, and `ShowOutput`.\n\nThe implementation emits Tauri events (`sky://output/*`) to the frontend, passing channel identifiers and payload data as JSON. `CreateOutputChannel` returns the assigned channel ID, while other operations trigger state updates or visibility toggles in the Sky workbench. These handlers complete the output panel IPC contract, enabling extensions to manage logging channels and display terminal-like output asynchronously.",
			"SHA": "4fef1677bec1ca93773b4a867f591969043e4b67"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T06:33:15Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1072,
				3
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Implement command registration and execution handlers\n\nIntroduce three new RPC handlers in `CocoonService` to complete the command lifecycle contract defined in the `Vine` protocol: `RegisterCommand`, `UnregisterCommand`, and `ExecuteContributedCommand`.\n\nThe implementation bridges the extension host and the native backend by:\n- Registering and unregistering command IDs via the `CommandExecutor` trait in `Service.environment`.\n- Marshaling protobuf `argument` oneofs (String, Int, Bool, Bytes) into `serde_json::Value` for flexible argument passing to the executor.\n- Executing commands asynchronously and returning results or structured errors (`RpcError`) as JSON bytes.\n- Adding detailed logging for command lifecycle events to aid debugging in the extension host environment.\n\nThis completes the bridge for user-initiated actions and extension commands, enabling extensions to register custom commands that trigger native logic or invoke other VS Code commands.",
			"SHA": "d53f35344835e6f664c0d88c40bdecda13954401"
		}
